{"tool_name":"anisotropic-diffusion-2d","contents":["neubias"],"fetched_metadata":{"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"markdown","processed":"","summary":"","value":">Anisotropic filters are a class of filter that reduces noise in an image while trying to preserve sharp edges\r\n\r\nThere are two implementations of Tschumperle/ R. Deriche filter (\"anisotropic diffusion\") for ImageJ Plugin \r\n\r\n1. in the \"imaging book\" codes: [see the javadoc here](https://imagingbook.github.io/imagingbook-common/javadoc/imagingbook/pub/edgepreservingfilters/TschumperleDericheFilter.html). \r\n\r\n2. in [Xlib](https://imagej.net/Xlib#Anisotropic_Diffusion)\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2018-12-18T03:30:34+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2013-10-11T13:08:41+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribution_instructions":[],"comments_2023":[],"free_tagging":[],"give_feedback_on_this_soft":[{"cid":0,"comment_count":0,"last_comment_name":null,"last_comment_timestamp":1505206276,"last_comment_uid":164,"status":2}],"has_author":[{"value":"Vladimir Pilny"},{"value":"Jiri Janacek"},{"value":"Johannes Schindelin"}],"has_biological_terms":[],"has_comparison":[],"has_documentation":[{"options":[],"title":"","uri":"https://imagej.nih.gov/ij/plugins/anisotropic-diffusion-2d.html"}],"has_doi":[],"has_entry_curator":[{"target_id":98,"target_type":"user","target_uuid":"2ae7ecac-ed23-4375-8a06-79f6a294e65b","url":"/user/98"}],"has_function":[{"target_id":4025,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"http://edamontology.org/operation_Image_smoothing","url":"/smoothing"}],"has_implementation":[{"target_id":4340,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"6077b127-35d6-45a8-ac32-b321e9bd18f2","url":"/taxonomy/term/4340"}],"has_interaction_level":[{"target_id":3573,"target_type":"taxonomy_term","target_uuid":"43cf6a59-36ad-49c8-9baa-3c5494481f13","url":"/taxonomy/term/3573"}],"has_license":[{"value":"GPLv3"}],"has_location":[{"options":[],"tit